// apps/spaces/deck.jsonc — the space scaffold defines the space scaffold.
//
// Per-app serve config (the `AppServeConfig` shape deck consumes). Loaded by
// shipd via the app-registration port; deck-config owns the schema + parser.
//
// Post deck-jsonc-simplify cutover, the file only carries the
// non-conventional bits. `name`/`route`/`source`/`render` moved to
// host-owned binds (apps.jsonc + convention):
//
//   - name   → derived from the directory basename (`apps/spaces` ⇒ `spaces`)
//   - route  → declared in apps.jsonc (`apps/shipd/apps.jsonc`) —
//              `route: "/space/{id}"` lives there, not here. The app does
//              not decide where it mounts.
//   - source → always `<root>/.deck` (the bundler's out_dir)
//   - render → defaults to csr
//
// What the file CAN carry (the only non-conventional pieces):
//
//   injectGlobals? { string: string }  window.<k>=<v>; `$<param>` tokens
//                                     substituted from the route's URL
//                                     path captures declared in
//                                     apps.jsonc. For the space
//                                     scaffold's `route: "/space/{id}"`,
//                                     `DECK_APP_ID: $id` resolves to
//                                     `window.DECK_APP_ID="<id>";` in
//                                     the served index.html.
//
//   entry? { clientsModule, exposeNames }   host-owned entry bootstrap the
//                                     bundler emits as `entry.gen.ts`: it
//                                     imports the data tables from
//                                     `routes.gen`, builds the named
//                                     `clients` map off `clientsModule`'s
//                                     exports, and calls `mountRouter`. Without
//                                     it the entry falls back to
//                                     `routes.gen.ts` (routes registered, but
//                                     nothing mounts). `exposeNames` become the
//                                     keys exposed to every view's
//                                     `ctx.<name>`.
{
  "injectGlobals": { "DECK_APP_ID": "$id" },
  "entry": {
    "clientsModule": "./src/lib/client.ts",
    "exposeNames": ["ship", "ops"]
  }
}
